{
  "text": "Hey Wenqing, I originally wanted to write this in Chinese, then I realized my skill was not up to par, so for everyone's sake, we're sticking to English. But if effort counts, just know that I did consider it. So I've been thinking about when all of this stopped feeling casual and started feeling real. Like the Renaissance Fair, our first full day date. Watching you try on all your little accessories, admiring yourself in the mirror, I remember just standing there, feeling strangely content, thinking you looked really happy, and really really cute. Then Yosemite, a 9 hour hike I was fully convinced I couldn't finish. Somewhere along the way my legs felt done and I remember wondering if I'd overestimated myself. But we kept going anyways, step after step, and somehow we made it. I don't think I would have finished that hike without you there. And that night, lying under the stars, talking about random things in my car, it didn't feel that long. But when we checked the time, two of us had somehow passed without either of us noticing. It felt easy, natural, peaceful in a way that's hard to put into words. And it's not just the big adventures, it's cooking together for the first time and acting like we're professionals. It's sitting on the couch, watching RCA drama, and getting way too invested in the action scenes. It's the small ordinary moments that don't feel ordinary when they're with you. We're different in a lot of ways and I don't pretend to know exactly what the future looks like. I just know what we have feels real to me. Being with you feels steady. It makes me feel content. And that's enough for me.",
